Center subject is SCP-5238-2-C33. Subject furthest right is SCP-5238-1-C33.



Special Containment Procedures:  Foundation agents imbedded in hospitals are to monitor the medical history of openly transgender and non-binary individuals for signs of SCP-5238 infection. Subjects believed to be instances of SCP-5238-2 are to be immediately relocated to Foundation emergency clinics for evaluation.

SCP-5238 and SCP-5238-2 instances are to be housed in standard humanoid containment. SCP-5238-2 subjects are to receive regular counseling and access to social privileges. Following SCP-5238 expiration, SCP-5238-2 instances are to be administered with amnestics and returned to the general population. If SCP-5238-2 previously cohabitated with SCP-5238-1, new accommodations are to be furnished.

SCP-5238 instances that have consumed SCP-5238-2 may also be housed in standard humanoid containment. Instances of SCP-5238 are to be allowed contact with their associated SCP-5238-1 instance daily for feeding purposes. If SCP-5238-1 cannot be accessed, staff are to initiate contact once daily and express approval of SCP-5238's new appearance and behavior.

Instances of SCP-5238-1 are to be housed in standard humanoid containment and monitored closely for thaumaturgic activity.

Due to global and regional disparities in access to and quality of healthcare for trans and non-binary people, as well as the social capability for such individuals to be open about their identity, detection of SCP-5238 activity is difficult. Further research into non-invasive methods of monitoring at-risk individuals is required.

Description:  SCP-5238 are parasitic organisms similar in appearance to enlarged human fetuses at a developmental stage of approximately seven weeks. Larval SCP-5238 instances are equipped with a jawless, toothed mouth and four hooklike claws on their underdeveloped appendages.

SCP-5238 may be summoned by women who have undergone menopause and are the parents of transgender or non-binary children. SCP-5238 eggs are manifested directly into the womb, causing the subject to become an instance of SCP-5238-1. The SCP-5238 summoning process has not yet been observed, and its mechanism is unknown. How SCP-5238-1 subjects become aware of SCP-5238's existence is also unclear. Circumstantial evidence suggests that SCP-5238 summoning events may be thaumaturgic or religious in nature. However, no texts outlining the procedure, nor Groups of Interest that promote the practice have been found.

SCP-5238 has a gestational period of approximately seven weeks. Upon hatching, the larval SCP-5238 instance exits the womb through the birth canal. It then makes its way to suitable offspring of SCP-5238-1 in an approximately 200-meter radius. During and after this process, a memetic camouflage effect renders perception of the SCP-5238 instance difficult or impossible for those not briefed on its effects. If no suitable hosts are present within its range, SCP-5238 will desiccate and expire.

SCP-5238 will attach itself to transgender or non-binary offspring of SCP-5238-1, hereby referred to as SCP-5238-2. Over a period of 5-6 days, SCP-5238 grows in size and engulfs SCP-5238-2 in a sheath of tissue. This sheath grows from the attachment site at the back of the neck, engulfs the head, and eventually covers the entire body. SCP-5238’s underdeveloped eye and mouth structures move to the front of SCP-5238-2’s head and become enlarged. Upon completion of this process, SCP-5238 is considered to have entered its adult phase.

At this stage, SCP-5238 instances will utilize their visual memetic abilities to conceal themselves and to modify SCP-5238-2's appearance. These modifications mimic the secondary characteristics of the sex assigned to SCP-5238-2 at birth. Cultural traits stereotypically associated with SCP-5238-2’s birth sex will also appear to manifest, such as gender-coded clothing, makeup, and hairstyle. If SCP-5238-2 had already possessed traits targeted by SCP-5238 for alteration, they will appear exaggerated. SCP-5238-2 will experience vague discomfort and dysphoria but is otherwise typically1 unaware of SCP-5238.

Anatomical changes to SCP-5238-2's appearance include, but are not limited to:

Gracilization or robustification of skeletal structure
Addition or subtraction of breast tissue
Addition or subtraction of body hair
Changes to distribution of fat and muscle tissue
Alteration of facial structure
Alteration of vocal pitch
Alteration of genitals


If SCP-5238-2 possesses a chosen name different from the one given to them at birth, they may become unable to use it in reference to themselves. Attempting to do so results in visible difficulty and compulsive repetition of their given name.

When SCP-5238-2’s head has become engulfed, direct respiration, as well as the direct consumption of food and drink, becomes impossible. SCP-5239 will provide SCP-5238-2 with an intravenous supply of oxygen, nutrition, and hydration, however the amounts supplied are suboptimal for survival. Over a period of nine months, SCP-5238-2 will slowly expire due to chronic hypoxia, dehydration, and malnutrition. After nine months have elapsed, SCP-5238 will incorporate SCP-5238-2’s biomass into itself.

SCP-5238 does not feed on SCP-5238-2 directly but instead exhibits a form of social brood parasitism. It is thought to subsist on positive attention paid to it by individuals close to SCP-5238-2 (especially SCP-5238-1) through anomalous means. SCP-5238 is especially receptive to approval and affirmation of traits and behaviors consistent with SCP-5238-2’s birth sex. To this end, SCP-5238 may influence and control SCP-5238-2’s behavior and psychology.

In some cases2, SCP-5238 may desiccate and slough off partway through the transformation process. This occurrence has been linked to individuals close to SCP-5238-2 expressing support and affirmation for SCP-5238-2’s chosen gender identity. Separation from SCP-5238-1 has been shown to accelerate the desiccation process. Trans-positive cultural attitudes surrounding SCP-5238-2 have also been liked to the incidence of SCP-5238 death.
