The remains recovered from SCP-5238-2-C33's residence were identified as a partial SCP-5238 instance. The instance had been sliced off of SCP-5238-2-C33's skin in pieces with a sharp instrument, possibly a razor blade. It had then been repeatedly stabbed and crushed underfoot. Much of SCP-5238-2-C33's epidermal tissue was removed along with the instance, along with two of 5238-2-C33's fingers. The final journal page, assumed by police to be a suicide note, was found crumpled among the remains.



Your daughter is dead.
附加记录：    

SCP-5238-2-C33 was missing for two months. On 1/12/92, Foundation investigators located 5238-2-C33 in Winthrop, Washington, recovering in a backwoods residence alongside one Robyn Joyce.

SCP-5238-1-C33 was successfully contained. A variety of Christian iconography, possibly ritualistic in nature, was found in her possession, alongside a burnt sample of what is believed to be SCP-5238-2-C33's umbilical cord.

SCP-5238-2-C33 was found to possess no anomalous properties. Amnestics were administered, and containment was deemed unnecessary.

